# Architecture

Feature layout: `domain/`, `data/`, `state/`, `presentation/`. Feature widgets live in `presentation/widgets/`. Create `state/` and `widgets/` only when the first Cubit or widget appears.

- `domain` does not import Flutter, Firebase, Dio, or `get_it`.
- `data` implements `domain`. `state` and `presentation` depend on `domain`, not on `data`.
- Cubit and Bloc classes live only in `state/`. Simple UI state uses Cubit. The widget that owns that state creates the Cubit.
- Read Cubit state with `BlocBuilder`. Do not use `context.watch`.
- Keep `build` methods small. Extract a nested widget when a builder covers more than one layout region.
- Resolve the graph in `main` via `configureDependencies`. `App` provides only app-wide cubits: theme, locale, and auth session.
- The router only maps a location to a screen. It does not take or pass feature dependencies.
- A screen reads each dependency it needs from `getIt` in `core/di/injection.dart`. Nested widgets do not call `getIt`.
- User-facing strings come from ARB (`lib/l10n`). Regenerate with `flutter gen-l10n`.
- Feature widgets read colors with `context.colors` and strings with `context.l10n`. Do not call `Theme.of(context).extension<AppColors>()` or `AppLocalizations.of(context)` in features.
- Shared widgets and theme settings live in `core/ui_kit/`.
- Presentation and state import Material, `flutter_bloc`, `go_router`, and `ui_kit` through `core/dependencies.dart`. Do not export Dio, Firebase, or `get_it` from that file.
- Value types and sealed states extend `Equatable` and put fields in `props`. Do not use `freezed` or hand-written `==`.
- Do not use the null-assertion operator `!` on a nullable value. Handle the missing value with `??`, a null check, or a pattern. Boolean `!` and `is!` are ordinary operators. Leave the `!` that `flutter gen-l10n` writes in `lib/l10n/generated/`.
- Call `Firebase.initializeApp` with `DefaultFirebaseOptions.currentPlatform` before `configureDependencies`.
- Codegen: `dart run build_runner build`.
- Write code comments and commit messages in English only. User-facing copy stays in the ARB files.
